From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:04:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] btrfs: complete the backport of the fix for false IO failures

The base backports upstream commit 66ff4d366e7e ("btrfs: fix false IO
failure after falling back to buffered write") as af1d826a8ac8, but
keeps passing false as uptodate to btrfs_finish_ordered_extent() in
btrfs_dio_iomap_end(), where upstream and its 7.1.y backport pass true.
So the ordered extent of a direct write range that was not submitted
still finishes as an IO error instead of only as truncated, and an
fsync that waits for it fails with EIO, for example after part of the
source buffer of a direct write could not be faulted in.

Fixes: af1d826a8ac8 ("btrfs: fix false IO failure after falling back to buffered write")
Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
---
 fs/btrfs/direct-io.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/btrfs/direct-io.c b/fs/btrfs/direct-io.c
index 58a19363955a1927ea387bbf3716020a1473cee3..5c6116f5fbb48adbf6cb93717aba0c1634d5a336 100644
--- a/fs/btrfs/direct-io.c
+++ b/fs/btrfs/direct-io.c
@@ -684,7 +684,7 @@ static int btrfs_dio_iomap_end(struct inode *inode, loff_t pos, loff_t length,
 			 */
 			btrfs_mark_ordered_extent_truncated(dio_data->ordered, 0);
 			btrfs_finish_ordered_extent(dio_data->ordered,
-						    pos, length, false);
+						    pos, length, true);
 		} else {
 			btrfs_unlock_dio_extent(&BTRFS_I(inode)->io_tree, pos,
 						pos + length - 1, NULL);
